    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick, mini.extra\n\n### Description\n\nI love mini.pick and would like to use it as a wrapper around vim.lsp.buf.definition to jump to definition, or select from one of many options in the case that the lsp detects more than one definition.\n\nI know that mini.extra already provides an LSP picker, but it currently will not automatically jump to definition even if there is one unambiguous one. I think it would be nice to have an option inside mini.pick (at pick.start for example) to specify whether \"auto-select-only-option\" is enabled, then mini.extra.pickers.lsp can depend on this to enable such behaviour for when querying for lsp definitions.",
