            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks foe the suggestion!\n\nThe similar use case was already discussed in #978 with the [following resolution](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/978#issuecomment-2178081844). So I don't think it is a good idea to add direct support for this use case.\n\nHowever, in case this might help, there is a way to add \"choose item if it is single\" behavior to any picker:\n\n```lua\nlocal autochoose_single = function()\n  local items = MiniPick.get_picker_items()\n  if #items ~= 1 then return end\n  local choose = MiniPick.get_picker_opts().source.choose or MiniPick.default_choose\n  vim.schedule(function() choose(items[1]) end)\n  MiniPick.stop()\nend\n\n-- NOTE: This relies on items being set synchronously, i.e. before start.\n-- To also work with async items setting (with a bit of performance penalty of\n-- being called more often), use 'MiniPickMatch' pattern.\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniPickStart', callback = autochoose_single })\n```",
            "created_at": "2025-09-10T11:23:21Z",
